ing_Angel.jpg/500px-Destroying_Angel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Young specimens like this are sometimes confused with puffballs or other non-deadly mushrooms.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADestroying_Angel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/500px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/1280px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Destroying_Angel_02.jpg/500px-Destroying_Angel_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A growing destroying angel (specifically the species Amanita virosa) in Ludvika, Sweden","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADestroying_Angel_02.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.433125},{"title":"2020-01-11 Ice hockey at the 2020 Winter Youth Olympics – Women's 3x3 mixed tournament – Preliminary round – Yellow vs. Grey (Martin Rulsch) 041","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/2020-01-11_Ice_hockey_at_the_2020_Winter_Youth_Olympics_%E2%80%93_Women%27s_3x3_mixed_tournament_%E2%80%93_Preliminary_round_%E2%80%93_Yellow_vs._Grey_%28Martin_Rulsch%29_041.jpg/500px-2020-01-11_Ice_hockey_at_the_2020_Winter_Youth_Olympics_%E2%80%93_Women%27s_3x3_mixed_tournament_%E2%80%93_Preliminary_round_%E2%80%93_Yellow_vs._Grey_%28Martin_Rulsch%29_041.jpg","ratio":1.786512